{"id": "0118d73492a2488d821e", "repository": "ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills", "commit_sha": "8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0", "skill_path": "skills/swot-analysis/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/blob/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/swot-analysis/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "a8ec2d46b1f3a111525441c375ad86e1476b417b", "sha256": "850954ff4b6d91c4635406932c144d5b69e0cb85afc8dc27ce405ee27b1a6b19", "bytes": 3259, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T10:53:46.428148+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/swot-analysis/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": ["LICENSE"], "repository_manifest": "manifests/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0.json", "local_package_files": ["skills/swot-analysis/SKILL.md", "skills/swot-analysis/references/example.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: swot-analysis\ndescription: >\n  Use for SWOT analysis, or when the user wants to assess where a team, product or company stands: \"strengths and weaknesses\", \"should we enter this market?\", \"review our position\", \"competitor comparison\". Turns findings into actions. Skip for detailed planning or pure market sizing.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: ysskrishna\n  version: \"2026.10.5\"", "declared_name": "swot-analysis", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "038331836a4198c88faa", "repository": "ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills", "commit_sha": "8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0", "skill_path": "skills/systems-thinking/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/blob/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/systems-thinking/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "8b82576f935a74c4591dab132e4fa4b2d504b0ed", "sha256": "97b4bc3567c12d4bc93f96592af0e3991aefd3982f9cca13f86186bc6f843acc", "bytes": 3340, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T10:53:46.428191+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/systems-thinking/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": ["LICENSE"], "repository_manifest": "manifests/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0.json", "local_package_files": ["skills/systems-thinking/SKILL.md", "skills/systems-thinking/references/example.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: systems-thinking\ndescription: >\n  Use for systems thinking, or when a change may ripple beyond its target: \"what are the side effects?\", \"why does this keep coming back?\", \"how do these teams or services affect each other?\". Maps loops, delays and leverage points. Skip for single-step fixes.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: ysskrishna\n  version: \"2026.10.5\"", "declared_name": "systems-thinking", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "6d47b22ed4ede227aeb9", "repository": "ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills", "commit_sha": "8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0", "skill_path": "skills/thinking-method-selector/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/blob/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/thinking-method-selector/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "991dc33f98f3b1d954f0465e5c8a293759c9655f", "sha256": "34d55771bb9886ac769a6343b3f228300e51de10c2ea0104720af71cef4668e5", "bytes": 7350, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T10:53:46.428232+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/thinking-method-selector/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": ["LICENSE"], "repository_manifest": "manifests/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0.json", "local_package_files": ["skills/thinking-method-selector/SKILL.md", "skills/thinking-method-selector/references/example.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: thinking-method-selector\ndescription: >\n  Use when the user describes a problem, decision or stuck situation but names no method: \"how should I approach this?\", \"help me think this through\", \"we can't decide\", \"where do I start?\". Picks the best-fit thinking method and runs it. Skip for plain execution tasks or when a method is named.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: ysskrishna\n  version: \"2026.10.5\"", "declared_name": "thinking-method-selector", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
{"id": "adbf22f8f03be150f71c", "repository": "ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills", "commit_sha": "8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0", "skill_path": "skills/tradeoff-analysis/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/blob/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/tradeoff-analysis/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "2f6ccfbe0fd5f341405260c433e7dc25ecb85f86", "sha256": "65b6bdf9e7346f50818a6ef5d748f79ab0f06f2403e066ee317d6ce0489e6261", "bytes": 3658, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T10:53:46.428277+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0/skills/tradeoff-analysis/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": ["LICENSE"], "repository_manifest": "manifests/ysskrishna/ai-agent-skills/8a6a5745556e60706ac5fa889dcc66ccd3a875b0.json", "local_package_files": ["skills/tradeoff-analysis/SKILL.md", "skills/tradeoff-analysis/references/example.md"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: tradeoff-analysis\ndescription: >\n  Use for tradeoff analysis, or when the user must pick between concrete options: \"A or B?\", \"which library should we use?\", \"build vs buy\", \"compare these approaches\". Scores options on weighted criteria, tests sensitivity and reversibility. Skip for open ideation or single-option reviews.\nlicense: MIT\nmetadata:\n  author: ysskrishna\n  version: \"2026.10.5\"", "declared_name": "tradeoff-analysis", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
